{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>To the large one you shall increase his inheritance.</b> In quantity of land. For the land was indeed divided into twelve equal portions in value, though not equal in quantity — rather, a kor of poor land against a se'ah of good. The tribe numerous in population received the portion large in quantity, and the tribe that was small received the portion small in quantity, equal in value to the portion large in quantity, as it says: לָרַב תַּרְבֶּה נַחֲלָתוֹ. In this manner Manasseh and Ephraim took two portions on account of the birthright of Joseph, as it says (Genesis 48:22): נָתַתִּי לְךָ שְׁכֶם אַחַד עַל אַחֶיךָ, and as is explained by (1 Chronicles 5:1): וּבְחַלְּלוֹ יְצוּעֵי אָבִיו נִתְּנָה בְכֹרָתוֹ לִבְנֵי יוֹסֵף בֶּן יִשְׂרָאֵל. And to Simeon, who had diminished in population more than all the other tribes at the time of their entry into the land, He gave a portion small in quantity but very precious in value. And since no single parcel of land was found sufficient for Simeon, they selected that portion in several places within the territory of Judah, as it says (Joshua 19:9): וּמֵחֶבֶל בְּנֵי יְהוּדָה נַחֲלַת בְּנֵי שִׁמְעוֹן. And thereby was fulfilled in the tribe of Simeon (Genesis 49:7): אֲחַלְּקֵם בְּיַעֲקֹב."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:17.043049674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}